          "path": "_m/g/c/k/y/barclodiad-y-gawres-wp/the-central-chamber-of-the-bar.jpg",
          "filename": "The central chamber of the Barclodiad-y-Gawres tomb - geograph.org.uk - 1059446.jpg",
          "caption": "The central chamber of the Barclodiad-y-Gawres tomb Excavations by Powell and Daniel in 1956 showed that a cremation fire had been lit in the central chamber. This fire had been extinguished once the flesh had been burnt with a soup made of fishes, frogs and field mammals. The site then had been \"carefully covered with limpet shells, so that all the bones survived\" (Frances Lynch Gwynedd HMSO 1995 pp12)",
          "alt": "The central chamber of the Barclodiad-y-Gawres tomb Excavations by Powell and Daniel in 1956 showed that a cremation fire had been lit in the central chamber. This fire had been extinguished once the flesh had been burnt with a soup made of fishes, frogs and field mammals. The site then had been \"carefully covered with limpet shells, so that all the bones survived\" (Frances Lynch Gwynedd HMSO 1995 pp12)",
