          "filename": "The entrance passage into the Barclodiad-y-Gawres Grave - geograph.org.uk - 1059412.jpg",
          "caption": "The entrance passage into the Barclodiad-y-Gawres Grave. Barclodiad y Gawres means \"the giantess' apron\". The grave dates back some 5000 years. The bunch of withering flowers in the passage suggests that the ashes of someone of our times have been scattered in the tomb.\n425549",
